From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:12:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: past the kept cap, shared-prefix states go by
 recency, TF_GLM_CAP_SHARED_RECENCY (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0077)

Past TF_GLM_CACHE_ENTRIES the multi-stream decoder drops a superseded kept prompt first (a state shorter than another
in its extent: recipe patch 0063). A run of an agent keeps its system block's shared-prefix state and its own longer
state in one extent, so once every other kept prompt is some conversation's latest state, the new run's system-block
state is the only superseded entry and goes at its next kept state, and the agent's next run reads its whole prompt
again (first token 14 s -> 40 s in the recipe's issue #75; a larger cap only delays it). MiaAI-Lab's recipe v1.7.1
drops a conversation's earlier non-shared states first, then the least recently used of any, with patch
0077-glm-kept-cap-shared-by-recency (the diagnosis and the fix proposed by meleesciony, issue #75). Which state is kept
only: the same replies. 2.0's configuration keeps up to 20 (TF_GLM_CACHE_ENTRIES=20), so its cap can fill the same
way (shown on the CPU below, with and without 0071's copy; not measured on the Sparks). This ports it behind a switch
of this tree's own, off by default:

- multi.py: cap_victim_recency, 0077's cap_victim verbatim (the tree's cap_victim stays, unchanged);
  MultiDecoder.cap_recency (TF_GLM_CAP_SHARED_RECENCY) picks it in _keep.
- engine.py: with --parallel, the switch in the ranks' startup row and in its refusal (both ranks drop the same kept
  prompt); a startup line when it is on.
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md: "GLM kept cap, shared by recency".

Unset, _keep drops cap_victim's choice, as before.

Tests: tests/test_glm_cap_recency.py (8, CPU): the switch; the order (0063's choice is the run's system-block state,
0077's the least recently used; a conversation's earlier non-shared state goes first under both); an agent's next run
with the cap at 3 and four kept states, two ranks over the fake model with and without TF_GLM_SHARED_PREFIX_COPY=1
(patch 0071) and the AFD attention node at world 1: off, the system-block state is dropped and the next run reads its
whole prompt; on, it is kept and the next run resumes the system block. Every reply equals the request served alone.

Credit: patch 0077 was written by MiaAI-Lab (https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab) in recipe commit 742a2cc (v1.7.1, pull
request #77), Apache License 2.0; the diagnosis and the fix were proposed by meleesciony
(https://github.com/meleesciony) in MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold issue #75.

Changed from the picked commit: tests/test_glm_shared_prefix.py's cap test (patch 0063's cap_victim against the
oldest-first rule) runs with TF_GLM_CAP_SHARED_RECENCY unset, since 0077's rule replaces 0063's when it is set.

